    "q-1129": {
      "dom_id": "step-q1129",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "If $-6{log}_{3}⁡(x-3)=-24$, then $x=$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange our equation to isolate the logarithmic term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{log}_{3}⁡(x-3) & =-24 \\\\ {log}_{3}⁡(x-3) & =\\frac{-24}{-6} \\\\ {log}_{3}⁡(x-3) & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo remove the logarithm, we exponentiate both sides of the equation. The base of the logarithm is $3,$ so we use this base for the exponentiation as well:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{3}⁡(x-3) & =4 \\\\ {3}^{{log}_{3}⁡(x-3)} & ={3}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since exponentiation is the inverse function of the logarithm, we get ${3}^{{log}_{3}⁡(x-3)}=x-3.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3 & ={3}^{4} \\\\ x-3 & =81 \\\\ x & =84.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
