    "q-79388": {
      "dom_id": "step-q79388",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "If $7{log}_{5}⁡x-2{log}_{5}⁡x=10$, then what is the value of  $x?$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we rearrange our equation to isolate the logarithmic term:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}7{log}_{5}⁡x-2{log}_{5}⁡x & =10 \\\\ (7-2){log}_{5}⁡x & =10 \\\\ 5{log}_{5}⁡x & =10 \\\\ {log}_{5}⁡x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo remove the logarithm, we exponentiate both sides of the equation. The base of the logarithm is $5,$ so we use this base for the exponentiation as well:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{log}_{5}⁡x & =2 \\\\ {5}^{{log}_{5}⁡x} & ={5}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since exponentiation is the inverse function of the logarithm, we get ${5}^{{log}_{5}⁡x}=x.$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={5}^{2} \\\\ x & =25.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-79388-a",
